1
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Hollywood Dirt is a drama, romance film directed by Tosca Musk.

2
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Hollywood arrives in force to Quincy, the small town where
the secret Crown Cola billionaire's live.

3
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:36,000
They want to film about the billionaire's and how they made their fortunes.

4
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:06,000
Summer Jenkins, who was the town pariah, joins forces with the scout, Ben, and finds filming
locations, extras, lessons with the town officials and house owners, etc.

5
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:36,000
When Cole Masten arrives, they hate each other, but sparks fly.

6
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Cole is running from a nasty divorce, yet is captivated by Summer.

7
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:36,000
Summer is dying to leave town to get away from the gossip.

8
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
This is a great story about Southern customs, a Southern
girl, and a Hollywood star who finds his lady.

9
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
Summer Jenkins, played by Emma Rigby.

10
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Cole Masten, played by Johann Urb.

11
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:36,000
Thelma, played by Mindy Cohn.

12
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Brad DeLuca, played by Marco Dapper.

13
01:11:30,000 --> 01:11:36,000
Stacy, played by Melissa LeEllen.

14
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
Mama, played by Beverly Leech.

15
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
The Dirt is a 2019 American biographical comedy-drama film directed by Jeff Tremaine and written
by Rich Wilkes and Amanda Adelson, about heavy metal/glam metal band Mötley Crüe.

16
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
The film stars Douglas Booth, Colson Baker, Daniel Webber and Iwan Rheon.

17
01:33:30,000 --> 01:33:36,000
Talks of a Mötley Crüe biopic began as early as 2006, when Paramount Pictures and MTV Films purchased the rights to the book The Dirt: Confessions of the World's Most Notorious Rock Band by the band and
Neil Strauss; however, the project then languished in development hell for over a decade, going through numerous directors and cast members before Netflix purchased the rights in March 2017.

18
01:39:00,000 --> 01:39:06,000
Filming began around New Orleans in February 2018.

19
01:44:30,000 --> 01:44:36,000
The Dirt was released digitally on Netflix on March 22, 2019.

20
01:50:00,000 --> 01:50:06,000
It received generally negative reviews from critics, who said the film would please fans but
that it hesitated "in handling the more troubling aspects of the band's history."

21
01:55:30,000 --> 01:55:36,000
The tone is emotional.
